ich  is essentially is the oil oxidized or  not  and you're 100 right most cod liver oils  on the market are probably highly  oxidized so  that is an important aspect that people  need to think about  with any omega-3 supplement i used  rosita  before i went to the carnivore diet and  then i cut out like  everything just to figure out what was  going on but i used rosita because they  were  yeah they had all that testing and there  were no other ingredients i know  some of the cod liver oil i was looking  at had other oils added as well  that i didn't want to be ingesting so  rosita did look pretty good  okay cool um and then  earlier you mentioned copper a little  bit so  for people on low carb diets or on  more you know carnivorous diets  do we get enough copper what is it for  like you don't really  hear a lot about copper i thought people  had too much copper but maybe  maybe that's wrong well a lot of the too  much copper is from people losing the  ability  to move copper around in the body from  metabolic dysfunction you start  having increases in iron and copper  even in alzheimer's yeah you start  losing the ability to move  um your minerals around so a lot of  times copper overload  is actually due to metabolic dysfunction  um  and so so copper and i don't want to  just single out copper there are  potential nutrients of concern  for carnivore and so calcium would be  one magnesium  um manganese boron for anyone really  and um in copper is another one unless  you're sourcing from oysters or liver  typically  and like like i mentioned copper is the  most  nutrient depleted mineral from foods  from non-regenerative farms  in both plant and animal foods so it is  a nutrient of concern and uh  we've published a couple papers on the  importance of copper  and essentially um you cannot move  iron around in the body without copper  so any  so we're even thinking that a lot of  iron deficiency anemia  is has nothing to do with not getting  enough iron it's actually